  "body": "In https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1466 we added the new \"perform a fetch\" hook for script fetching. However, @annevk raised some concerns that we are just layering too many hooks into the algorithms. I think this is a fair concern.\n\nIn reality, I think the issue is that consumers in general need to control the fetch. Our previous \"set up the request\" and \"process the response\" hooks were just subsets of the general functionality of \"perform a fetch\". It would be clearer if we just had one hook.\n\nWe should consolidate all hooks into one. But in doing so, we should be sure to update the service worker spec with a pull request, since they currently use the \"set up the request\" and \"process the response\" hooks, and it is not nice to change things out from under them.\n",
